# What must NOT be published to the public web (GL-079)
#
# Vercel serves this repository from its ROOT, so until this file existed every
# committed file was reachable at https://goodliquidbevco.com/<path>. Confirmed
# live on 2026-09-16, all returning 200:
#
#   /docs/database/authorization-baseline.txt   113 KB — every RLS policy
#                                               expression, table grant, and
#                                               SECURITY DEFINER function with
#                                               its exact signature and ACL
#   /docs/plans/technical-debt.md                69 KB — the defect register,
#                                               including issues still OPEN
#   /CLAUDE.md, /SECURITY.md, /CRM_FEATURE_MAP.md
#   /scripts/security-invariants.sh             the probe that guards the site
#   /supabase/migrations/*.sql                  the entire schema history
#   /supabase/functions/**/*.ts                 edge function source
#   /tests/*.test.cjs
#
# NO CREDENTIALS WERE EXPOSED. .gitignore keeps supabase/secrets.env and every
# .env out of the repository, so they were never uploaded; /supabase/secrets.env
# returned 404 and a scan of all 95 shipped scripts found no key material. The
# only key in the page is the publishable one, which is meant to be public.
#
# So this is reconnaissance, not a breach: RLS is the enforcement, and RLS holds
# -- an anonymous visitor was refused on 29 of 30 tables and every portal RPC.
# Obscurity is not what protects this database. But there is no reason to hand
# an attacker the function inventory to probe, the migration history to diff,
# and a register that names the weaknesses we already know about and have not
# yet fixed. Defence in depth means not volunteering the map.
#
# WHAT THE SITE ACTUALLY NEEDS, verified before writing this by extracting every
# src= and href= from all six HTML entry points: src/ (91 modules), the
# root-level .js and .css files, the icons and manifest. Nothing shipped
# references any path below. Keep it that way -- if a page ever needs a file
# from one of these directories, move the file rather than deleting the rule.

# Internal engineering documentation
docs/
prompts/
*.md

# Tooling that never runs in the browser
scripts/
tests/
tools/
.github/

# Database and edge-function source. Migrations are applied through the
# Supabase MCP and functions are deployed by CI, so neither is needed here.
# NOTE: supabase.min.js lives at the ROOT and is deliberately not matched.
supabase/

# Agent and editor state
.claude/
AGENTS.md
